# Line-ending policy (ADR-046: qualification must not be host-shaped).
#
# Every gate in this repository is a shell script, and `core.autocrlf=true` — the Git default on a
# Windows install — checks those scripts out with CRLF. A CRLF `#!/usr/bin/env bash` line makes the
# kernel look for an interpreter literally named "bash\r", and the gate dies with
#
#     env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#
# before it runs a single check. That is not a Windows problem: the same clone shared into WSL, a
# container, or a VM fails identically. Since ADR-046 makes a Windows workstation a first-class
# place to run the x86-64 qualification, the executable text in this repo must be LF everywhere,
# regardless of the developer's global Git configuration.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.s       text eol=lf
*.ld      text eol=lf
*.toml    text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.rs      text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf

# Binary fixtures must never be touched by end-of-line conversion — a WASM module with its 0x0d
# bytes rewritten is a corrupt module, and the failure surfaces as a validation error far from the
# cause.
*.wasm    binary
*.efi     binary
*.img     binary
*.vdi     binary
*.vmdk    binary
